  "summary": "A distinctive Balinese textile created through the ikat weaving technique with characteristic diagonal patterns.",
  "description": "Endek textiles feature distinctive diagonal or zigzag patterns created through the warp ikat technique, where threads are tie-dyed before weaving. These textiles are used for everyday and ceremonial clothing in Bali, with patterns that often incorporate natural motifs and reflect Balinese Hindu cosmology and agricultural cycles.",
